  "missing": [],
  "caveats": [
    "hwserver (PID 2888, started 2026-10-25 00:47 by the b7 retry) was already listening on 127.0.0.1:5555 and was reused; no second hwserver was started and no Flash path was touched.",
    "At session start T: was still mapped to T10.b7-cam-diag/r0/td and an orphan td_commands_prompt.exe (PID 4500, created 2026-10-24 17:43, command ./01b_route_only.tcl) was still alive. td_env.ps1 -Force remapped T: to the b8 r0/td; b7 was already closed out and no TD build was running against it. The orphan was left untouched (not this task's process).",
    "F1 (finding, not a b8 change): the vendor fpga/csi2/prj/camera_peer/.../csi_rx_10bit_unpack.v mis-orders bytes when a 5-byte RAW10 group straddles a 32-bit word (evidence: sim/logs/sim_pipe_vendor_unpack.log). It is NOT in the P2 build - 01_build.tcl adds csi_rx_10bit_unpack_checked.v - so the real-pipe vector was run against the pair the candidate actually builds (csi_rx_packet_integrity + csi_rx_10bit_unpack_checked), CRC16 and keep semantics included.",
    "F2 (finding, out of b8 write scope): the built tap produces O_data_out = {p3,p2,p1,p0} (four 10-bit samples, p0 in [9:0]) while a1_frame_top documents its in_pix field order as [7:0]=b0 .. [39:32]=b4 (the five-byte RAW10 group layout used by the P1 testbench). The crop passes the 40-bit beat through unchanged either way, so geometry is unaffected, but the RAW/xform byte layout handed to the codec may not be the documented order. Needs a planner decision before any image-quality claim; no frozen module was changed in b8.",
    "Board (G4) NOT MET: the single authorised SRAM download succeeded (PRG-2014 + B8D_DL_OK mode=jtag(sram), 36.5 s) but the camera delivered no payload anywhere in the 90 s capture (cam_pix_beats=0, cam_line_rises=0, one stale FS/FE -> crop_short=1, crop_geom_err=0), so cap_frames/raw_pub/enc_frames/exported stayed 0 and no A1U1 frame existed to decode. The 90 s capture started 2 s before the download.",
    "Control for the board state: a 90 s COM8 capture taken immediately BEFORE the download, while the previous b7 bitstream was still loaded (captures/com8_90s_predownload_b7bit.bin, 90 v2 packets), shows the identical dead camera state (cam_pix_beats=0, cam_line_rises=0, cam_frame_rises=1, crop_short=1, crop_geom_err=0, cam_phystat OR 0x1EE, cam_sysstat OR 0x0F1D, all legacy counters 0). The sensor was already stopped (b7 saw it stop ~13 s after its own download) before b8 was loaded, so this is a board/sensor state, not a b8 regression. A user-side power cycle of the camera/board is required before a new 1-download round.",
    "Two extra COM8 captures (captures/com8_90s_predownload2_b7bit.*) were taken while a TD command path was mangled by Tcl backslash escapes (the download never opened the cable: 'couldn't read file'). No download byte was written in those attempts; the single real download is the one logged in board/download_sram_b8.log. The correct invocation needs forward slashes in the .tcl argument.",
    "Simulation-only value assertion in a1_raw_crop is guarded by `ifdef SIMULATION; the hard contract is a generate-based elaboration failure, so an illegal geometry cannot reach TD and TD never sees $finish.",
    "P1 goldens are read (read-only) from T10.b5-a1-htab-pipe/r0/sim/captures; b5/b7 packages were not modified.",
    "The pipe testbench checks OG*H = 128 ROI groups (16 rows x 8 groups): the design guide's '8x8' shorthand contradicts the frozen H=16; the frozen parameter table was treated as authoritative and every group is checked."
  ],
